  "description": "meme-id: white_people_after_10_shots_black_people_after_10_shots; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two images: the top image shows two white men drinking shots in a bar with a wild, uninhibited expression, labeled 'white people after 10 shots,' while the bottom image shows a Black man in formal attire smiling and holding a glass of what appears to be whiskey, labeled 'black people after 10 shots.' The intent is to imply that Black people are more composed, restrained, or 'professional' even after consuming alcohol, while white people are depicted as wild or out of control. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that reinforces racist tropes by suggesting inherent behavioral differences based on race, portraying Black people as overly composed or 'too good' to be wild, while white people are depicted as naturally rowdy. The meme uses racial categorization to make a derogatory comparison, which is a form of racialized stereotyping and can be interpreted as a subtle form of racial hierarchy. The overall intent is to perpetuate a harmful racial stereotype by implying that Black people are more 'in control' or 'professional' than white people in social situations, which is a form of racialized stereotyping and can be interpreted as a subtle form of racial hierarchy.",
